what Python's re does with a recursive pattern
  (?R)     refused at compile time
  (?1)     refused at compile time
  (?&p)    refused at compile time
  \g<0>    refused at compile time

counting instead
  (a(b)c)    balanced, offsets 0..6
  ((a)(b))   balanced, offsets 0..7
  ()         balanced, offsets 0..1
  (a(b)c     1 unclosed '(', outermost at offset 0
  a)b        unexpected ')' at offset 1
  a          no parentheses

no engine limit applies: depth is just an integer
  depth 10      balanced, offsets 0..20
  depth 1000    balanced, offsets 0..2000
  depth 100000  balanced, offsets 0..200000

and hostile input is answered in one pass, not searched
  ((((((((((((...  40 unclosed '(', outermost at offset 0
